title: Microsoft Hyper-V Cluster: Disk state
agents: windows
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the state of the physical disk resources of a Microsoft
 Windows failover cluster running Hyper-V.

 The check is {OK} if the disk is online, {WARN} if it is initializing, pending
 or going online or offline, {CRIT} if it is offline or failed and {UNKNOWN}
 for any other state.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_cluster.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V".

item:
 The name of the cluster disk resource.

discovery:
 One service is created for each cluster disk resource.

cluster:
 Every node of the failover cluster reports all cluster disks, so without a
 Checkmk cluster host the services are created on every node. In a Checkmk
 cluster host the report of the first node, in the order of the node names,
 is used.
